(a) whether Government has conducted a recent assessment of population of Gangetic river dolphins in the Brahmaputra river;
(b) if so, the details of conservation measures undertaken;
(c) whether any additional funds have been sanctioned for dolphin habitats in Assam; and
(d) if so, the details thereof, the projects undertaken and the status of their implementation?

(a) whether the Ministry proposes a dedicated programme for flood-resilient community infrastructure in upper Assam;
(b) if so, the details of districts identified therefor;
(c) the funds proposed under PM-DevINE or NESIDS  therefor; and
(d) the implementation schedule proposed therefor?

(a) the districts of Assam affected by floods resulting from cloudbursts in Arunachal Pradesh and Nagaland;
(b) the district-wise details of untimely deaths in Assam due to cloudbursts and floods during July, 2026;
(c) whether post-mortem examinations were conducted for all victims; and
(d) the details of financial ex-gratia or administrative assistance provided to the families of the deceased?

(a) whether Government has examined the nutritional status of beneficiaries residing in Tea garden areas of Assam under the Public Distribution System;
(b) whether any region-specific nutritional intervention is under consideration;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the expected beneficiaries?

(a) whether Government proposes to establish a nano-fertilizer manufacturing or distribution hub in Assam to serve the North Eastern region;
(b) the present status of the proposal;
(c) the estimated investment involved; and
(d) the expected benefits for farmers and fertilizer availability?

(a) whether Government proposes to install Battery Energy Storage Systems (BESS) in the State of Assam for improving grid reliability;
(b) the projects approved;
(c) the funds allocated; and
(d) the expected completion schedule with complete details?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of fertilizer-use efficiency in the production of paddy, wheat and pulses and its impact on productivity, soil health and input costs;
(b) the year-wise production of these food grains during the last five years, along with the quantity of chemical fertilizers consumed;
(c) the schemes implemented to promote balanced nutrient management, improve productivity and encourage sustainable farming practices; and
(d) the quantity and value of food grains exported during the last five years, the foreign exchange earned therefrom and the measures taken to enhance India's export competitiveness while ensuring domestic food security?

(a) whether Government proposes to establish India's first Tea Genome Research Centre in Assam to undertake genomic research on indigenous tea varieties;
(b) whether any proposal has been received from research institutions;
(c) the estimated financial outlay; and
(d) the expected contribution towards improving tea productivity, climate resilience and exports?

(a) whether Government proposes to establish dedicated skill development centres in tea garden areas of Assam;
(b) the number of youth trained and employed under central skill schemes in Assam during the last three years;
(c) whether industry-specific training in food processing, logistics, tourism and renewable energy is proposed; and
(d) the steps taken to improve employment opportunities for tea garden youth?

(a) whether Government proposes to establish modern pig breeding and pork processing centres in Assam;
(b) the financial assistance provided under various livestock schemes during the last three years;
(c) whether there is any proposal to promote indigenous pig breeds through scientific breeding; and
(d) the steps taken to increase employment and exports from the piggery sector in Assam?

(a) when, where and how Pradhan Mantri Jeevan Jyoti Bima Yojana (PMJJBY) and Pradhan Mantri Suraksha Bima Yojana (PMSBY) were officially launched;
(b) the core features, targets and primary objectives behind the introduction of both insurance schemes;
(c) the mechanism through which the general public can derive direct benefits from these two schemes; and
(d) the essential eligibility criteria prescribed for the public to qualify and the detailed step-by-step application process required to avail these benefits?

(a) the total number of household toilets constructed under Government sanitation schemes during the last five years, year-wise and State/UT-wise;
(b) the funds allocated and expenditure incurred for the same;
(c) whether Government proposes to provide household toilets to poor families still lacking such facilities, along with the eligibility criteria and implementation strategy;
(d) the point-wise eligibility conditions prescribed for beneficiaries; and
(e) whether toilets are constructed by beneficiaries themselves or through contractors/agencies, along with the guidelines and implementation mechanism governing such construction?

(a) whether any framework exists for the priority allotment of confirmed train tickets to critically ill patients requiring long-distance travel, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the specific application procedure and channels available for patients or their families to request emergency reservation confirmations;
(c) the mandatory medical certificates or documentary proofs required to validate and process these emergency travel requests; and
(d) whether this emergency ticket allocation facility is uniformly applicable across all train categories and accommodation classes?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any outcome-based assessment of the Pradhan Mantri Dhan-Dhanya Krishi Yojana (PMDDKY) since its launch, indicating its objectives and the measurable improvements in agricultural productivity and farmers' income;
(b) the budget allocation, funds released and expenditure under the Scheme, year-wise;
(c) the number of beneficiaries, including the category of benefits provided, State-wise; and
(d) whether Assam has been covered under the Scheme, if so, the district-wise number of beneficiaries, assistance provided, impact on farm productivity and income and the steps taken to expand the Scheme in the State?

(a) whether Government proposes a Brahmaputra Flood Forecasting and Climate Resilience Mission for Assam;
(b) whether Artificial Intelligence-based flood prediction and early warning systems are proposed;
(c) whether district-level climate monitoring centers would be established; and
(d) if so, the implementation schedule thereof?

(a) whether Government proposes to establish Smart Integrated Disaster and Emergency Response Centres in flood-prone districts of Assam;
(b) whether Artificial Intelligence-based flood forecasting systems are proposed;
(c) the financial support proposed for the project; and
(d) the districts likely to be covered?

(a) whether Government has assessed the gap between annual milk production, domestic demand and value-added dairy processing capacity during the last five years and, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the State-wise details of milk-based processing industries, their installed capacity, utilisation and employment generated;
(c) the measures taken to promote modern dairy processing, value addition, cold-chain infrastructure and entrepreneurship, particularly in the North Eastern Region; and
(d) whether Government proposes a region-specific strategy to strengthen milk production, processing, marketing and rural livelihoods, and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the date of launch, objectives and salient features of the Pradhan Mantri Jeevan Jyoti Bima Yojana (PMJJBY); 
(b) the eligibility criteria and enrolment procedure under the scheme;
(c) the total number of beneficiaries enrolled since its inception, year-wise and State/UT-wise, along with the number of claims settled;
(d) the measures taken to increase enrolment among farmers, agricultural labourers, unorganised workers and economically weaker sections; and 
(e) whether any awareness campaign or action plan has been implemented to achieve maximum coverage of eligible citizens and the progress made thereunder?

(a) whether Government provides dedicated financial assistance to underprivileged families undergoing treatment for critical illnesses, and if so, the details thereof;
(b) the maximum financial coverage ceiling and list of critical diseases permissible under the Ayushman Bharat Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY) Scheme;
(c) whether empanelled private nursing homes are mandated to accept Ayushman cards for cashless treatment;
(d) the criteria and specific socio-economic conditions fixed for a beneficiary to acquire an Ayushman card; and
(e) the operational guidelines and application procedure to avail financial aid under the Rashtriya Arogya Nidhi Scheme?

(a) the measures taken for sustainable management of the Brahmaputra basin and drinking water supply in the State of Assam;
(b) the status of Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM) implementation in Assam and other North Eastern States;
(c) the funds released during the last five years; and
(d) the steps taken to mitigate flood-related drinking water contamination?

(a) the present physical and financial progress of the Furkating–New Tinsukia multi-phase track doubling project under the Northeast Frontier Railway;
(b) whether engineering contracts have been awarded for the Bhojo–New Tinsukia section, if so, the targeted timeline for its completion and commissioning;
(c) the measures taken to enhance line capacity and increase the operational speed of passenger and freight trains towards Dibrugarh and Murkongselek; and
(d) whether Government proposes to introduce direct rail connectivity or additional Vande Bharat/Amrit Bharat trains connecting Upper Assam with other Northeastern States?

(a) whether Government proposes to establish a Food Processing Industry Training Centre in Dibrugarh or Tinsukia district of Assam to promote entrepreneurship and skill development;
(b) whether Government has assessed the growing demand for trained manpower in pork and poultry processing in Upper Assam, where consumption and small-scale enterprises are increasing;
(c) whether any survey has been conducted regarding training requirements of local entrepreneurs; and
(d) the steps proposed to provide technical training, food safety certification, value addition and marketing support to entrepreneurs in the region?

(a) the names of Heads of Nation/Government who have paid official visits to India during the last five years;
(b) whether any Agreements or Memoranda of Understanding (MoUs) relating to economic cooperation, infrastructure, industrial development, trade, technology or investment were signed during such visits and, if so, the country-wise details thereof;
(c) whether similar development and investment-related agreements were concluded during the Hon'ble Prime Minister's foreign visits during the same period; and
(d) whether any such agreements provide for investments in Assam and, if so, the sector-wise details, present status and timeline for implementation?

(a) whether the Prime Minister of Japan has recently paid an official visit to India and, if so, the major outcomes relating to economic cooperation and development;
(b) whether any Agreements or Memoranda of Understanding (MoUs) for infrastructure, industrial, technology, energy or other development-related investments were signed during the visit and, if so, the sector-wise details thereof;
(c) whether Assam has been included under any such investment proposals and, if so, the project-wise details thereof; and
(d) the present status and implementation timeline along with the steps taken by Government to expedite these development projects in Assam?

(a) the details of Government schemes implemented for senior citizens and Persons with Disabilities (PwDs) in Assam and other North Eastern States;
(b) the funds sanctioned and released during the last five years;
(c) the district-wise beneficiaries; and
(d) whether new rehabilitation centres are proposed in the region?

(a) the number of Gram Panchayats in Assam connected with the e-GramSwaraj portal;
(b) whether all Gram Panchayats have access to broadband and digital public services;
(c) the funds provided for strengthening Panchayati Raj Institutions (PRI) in Assam during the last five years; and
(d) the steps taken to improve digital governance in rural areas?

(a) whether Government proposes to establish a National Heatwave Health Preparedness Framework for public hospitals;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether any standard treatment protocol has been issued for heat-related illnesses; and
(d) the measures proposed to strengthen emergency healthcare facilities in heat-vulnerable districts?

(a) the details of AYUSH hospitals, dispensaries, medical colleges and Health & Wellness Centres functioning in Assam and the other North Eastern States, State-wise;
(b) the details of projects sanctioned under the National AYUSH Mission (NAM) in Assam during the last five years;
(c) the funds sanctioned, released and utilized for these projects, year-wise; and
(d) whether Government proposes to establish additional AYUSH hospitals, medical colleges or research institutes in Assam and the North Eastern Region, and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of MSME schemes implemented for bamboo, handloom and handicraft industries in the State of Assam and other North Eastern States;
(b) the number of enterprises assisted under these schemes;
(c) the financial assistance provided during the last five years; and
(d) the employment generated through these initiatives?
